---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="FAQ - Chauncy" description="Answers to questions buyers actually ask: privacy, AI, ingestion, refunds, system requirements, and how Chauncy fits next to tools you already use.">

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container faq-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Straight answers</p>
      <h1>Frequently asked questions.</h1>
      <p class="faq-sub">If your question isn't here, email <a href="mailto:support@chauncy.dev">support@chauncy.dev</a>. We answer.</p>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>Privacy and Data</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What stays on my machine?</summary>
            <p>Everything that matters. Your documents, the text Chauncy extracts from them, the search index, the embeddings, and your annotations all live on your local disk. Chauncy doesn't require an account, doesn't phone home, and doesn't track usage.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What leaves my machine, and when?</summary>
            <p>Two things, both only when you initiate them:</p>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>URL ingestion</strong> — when you paste a URL, Chauncy fetches the page from the web. The request goes out, the page comes back, Chauncy indexes it. After that, no further network activity on that document.</li>
              <li><strong>AI synthesis</strong> — if you turn AI on, only the excerpts Chauncy selects to answer your specific question are sent to your chosen provider, and only when you ask. Your full collection, index, and annotations stay local. If you use Ollama or a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint, nothing leaves the machine at all.</li>
            </ol>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Does Chauncy work without an internet connection?</summary>
            <p>Yes for search, indexing, and AI synthesis using a local model such as Ollama or a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The internet is needed only for URL ingestion, cloud AI providers, and voice input, which uses your system's speech recognition and may require network.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Do I need to create an account?</summary>
            <p>No. Buy the installer through Stripe, install it, run it. No account, no login, no profile.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>AI and Costs</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Do I need an AI API key to use Chauncy?</summary>
            <p>No. Chauncy's semantic search works without any AI provider. AI synthesis is optional — turn it on when you want it, leave it off when you don't.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>If I want AI, what does it cost?</summary>
            <p>Whatever your chosen provider charges. Chauncy uses your own API key with Anthropic or OpenAI; you pay the provider directly for what you use. Chauncy doesn't mark up provider costs, doesn't route your requests through our servers, and doesn't see your prompts or responses. If you run a local model with Ollama or a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint, there's no provider cost at all — just the hardware you already own.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What's involved in setting up a local AI model?</summary>
            <p>Chauncy doesn't bundle a local AI model. To use one, you install model-serving software on your own machine and download a model that fits your hardware. Ollama is a common choice. Chauncy connects to the running model through its local API. The setup is well documented by those projects and typically takes a short session to complete. If you'd rather skip the setup, cloud providers and search-only mode are available without any of this.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>What Chauncy Does</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What file formats can I ingest?</summary>
            <p>PDF, Word (.docx), PowerPoint (.pptx), Markdown, HTML/HTM, plain text, and email files (.eml, .mbox). Web pages can be ingested by pasting a URL.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How does Chauncy fit next to tools I already use?</summary>
            <p>Different tools, different jobs.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Note-taking and PKM tools</strong> ask you to build a knowledge graph by hand — tagging, backlinking, naming things consistently. Chauncy doesn't ask for that work. It infers the structure from the meaning of what you've written.</li>
              <li><strong>Desktop search tools</strong> match keywords. Chauncy matches meaning. A search can find a relevant document even when it shares no keywords with your query.</li>
              <li><strong>Read-it-later services</strong> save articles to read. Chauncy makes the things you've saved anywhere searchable by meaning.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>You can use Chauncy alongside any of these. Chauncy is the layer that lets you find and synthesize across what you've collected, however you collected it.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Can I have multiple separate libraries?</summary>
            <p>Not at launch. Chauncy supports one collection per installation. You can ingest from many folders, mailboxes, and URLs, but everything lands in the same searchable library.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>Buying and Using</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What does $99 get me?</summary>
            <p>A perpetual license to install and use Chauncy on computers you own or control, plus all updates within the current major version. New major versions may carry separate pricing; existing customers are notified in advance.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What are the system requirements?</summary>
            <p>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. 4 GB RAM minimum, 8 GB recommended for larger collections. Roughly 1 GB free disk for the application and runtime, plus space for your indexed content as it grows. No GPU required.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Is there a Mac version?</summary>
            <p>Not yet. macOS support is in development. There's a waitlist in the footer.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What if Chauncy isn't right for me?</summary>
            <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@chauncy.dev">support@chauncy.dev</a> with the subject "Refund Request" within 14 days of your purchase. No explanation required. Refunds are processed within 3-5 business days through Stripe back to your original payment method.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-cta">
        <p>Still have questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@chauncy.dev">support@chauncy.dev</a>. We answer.</p>
        <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-primary">Buy Chauncy for Windows - $99</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .faq-container {
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .faq-container h1 {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.8rem);
  }

  .faq-sub {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .faq-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .faq-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  details {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  details[open] {
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  summary {
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  summary::marker {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  details p,
  details li,
  .faq-cta p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  details ul,
  details ol {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  details strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .faq-cta {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .faq-cta .btn {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
